  "result": "I wrote the concept body and the three witnesses, but the gate never judged them: both runs returned `SCOPE_VIOLATION` because of files the shell tool creates, not anything I edited. That also means I haven't seen the files build or the witnesses pass.\n\n**What went wrong:** every time the shell tool runs a command, it saves the output to a file under `.runtime/tmp/claude-154266/.../tasks/` (here `bg10asrf8.output` and `bbe1co7r1.output`). That folder is inside the repository the gate checks, so it counts each one as a change outside the concept's files. Each gate run makes a new one, so I stopped after 2 of the 6 runs. I can't delete the two files (the shell only runs the gate command and I have no delete tool), so the harness's own final run may flag them too. The fix belongs in the harness: either ignore `.runtime/tmp` or keep that folder outside the repository.\n\n**The body** (`library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/interaction/overtake_pass.lean`):\n- **Behind:** b is behind a now, meaning the bearing's longitudinal component is negative and `rel_longitudinal_overlap` is below zero.\n- **Previous observation:** b had not been behind a at any point since it was last ahead with headings aligned. The language has no \"previous observation\" operator, so I wrote this as `rises(¬since(¬behind, aheadAligned))`, which gives the same thing on the instant b is behind. It also covers the contract's rule that the concept \"doesn't hold again until b has again been ahead and then comes to be behind\".\n- **Window:** the last ahead-and-aligned observation falls inside the time window, written as `atLast .time window … aheadAligned tt`, so a pass longer than the window is not recognized.\n\nAll three claimed atoms are used, zero is the only literal, and there are no narrowings because the contract settled every choice.\n\n**The witnesses:** the window is 6 s and `same_dir_cos` is 9/10.\n- **holds** (checked at t = 15 s): b starts ahead and aligned. At 12 s a is angled 37° while changing lanes, so b is ahead but not aligned. At 13 s and 14 s a is alongside b. At 15 s b is 3 m behind a, 4 s after the onset at 11 s.\n- **fails:** a pulls alongside b and stops there, so b is never behind a.\n- **blind:** the holds trace with `rel.bearing` hidden, also checked at t = 15 s.\n\nThe 12 s and 14 s scenes are there so that every condition in the body changes the holds result, which should avoid a `VACUOUS` verdict.\n\nI found no problem with the record itself. Everything is written up in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
